{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1368128-victorian-lost-2e","id":1368128,"title":"Victorian Lost 2e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-15T14:16:04-08:00","id":1368128,"title":"Victorian Lost 2e?","content":"So recently I have started getting into the Chronicles of Darkness rules system. I have previously run Vampire 20th over several campaigns and plan on running Vampire 5th as well so the rules are fairly familiar to me.<br /> I wanted to use the CoD 2e system over a series of short campaigns but my main setting is an analog of the victorian era (in a fantasy world) and I am finding (even in the dark eras books but I might just be looking in the wrong place) a lack of support for fully utilizing this time.<br /> Is there a Victorian Lost 2e planned at all?<br /> How easily could I use the VL 1e in CoD 2e? Are there any troubles with conversions that need to be made?<br /> Are there any other resources I can utilize out there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T10:54:49-08:00","id":1368329,"title":"","content":"OPP isn't really in the business of doing official 2e ports of 1e material. You'd unfortunately have to do any conversions yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T16:25:35-08:00","id":1368428,"title":"","content":"Which isn't to say that none of the mechanical content will ever get updated, but there won't likely be a Victorian Lost 2.0. Especially because most of the lore should still work regardless of edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T17:01:54-08:00","id":1368432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corelogic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1368128-victorian-lost-2e#post1368128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How easily could I use the VL 1e in CoD 2e? Are there any troubles with conversions that need to be made?</div> </div> </div> </div> The vast, vast majority of the book is fluff/lore rather than mechanics, and requires no such thing as &quot;conversion.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>However</i>, it is firmly a book about changelings in the Victorian period; if you're running something else, you'd be better served by just doing some cursory research elsewhere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T12:26:17-08:00","id":1368613,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2500\" data-vbnamecard=\"2500\">Corelogic</a> check out the Grimm Dark Era section in the Chronicles of Darkness - Dark Eras book. It's a 2e book. It isn't about Victorian England specifically, but it is about the 19th and early 20th century and even includes a new Seeming tied to that era, so it will certainly contain material useful to you if you plan on running an updated Victorian Lost chronicle.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> If you also own Dark Eras - Companion, also check out the Lifting the Veil chapter in that book. It contains more fluff and some optional rules and game mechanics for the Victorian era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","user":"Tomorrow's Nobody","date":". 02-17-2020, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T15:33:09-08:00","id":1368640,"title":"","content":"Victorian Lost should pretty much work fine with CTL Second Edition. The setting hasn't changed in any way that undermines its setting and narrative content. The two new kiths use rules that don't break in the 2e system. The new Contract rules won't port over, but there are only two pages' worth and you miss little. The sample stats for characters in the back don't line up to 2e Contract, Clarity, or Defense rules.<br /> <br /> The Grimm Dark Era does not use CTL Second Edition rules, unfortunately. It uses prototypical rules from the then in-development CTL Second Edition before CTL 2e changed developers and consequentially went in a very different direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T18:28:09-08:00","id":1368659,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies. Noticed that Victorian Lost was a changeling book only after I posted T__T.<br /> Mainly I am interested in running a humans versus humans and the supernatural game in a victorian time period.<br /> Using the CoD 2e book I think the area I am most lacking in is supernatural merits for humans. I would love to see this expanded upon (not specifically numina though but that might be interesting as well) and just items in general (which I can probably just come up with using a few lists that are out there).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T18:31:57-08:00","id":1368660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corelogic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1368128-victorian-lost-2e?p=1368659#post1368659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the replies. Noticed that Victorian Lost was a changeling book only after I posted T__T.<br /> Mainly I am interested in running a humans versus humans and the supernatural game in a victorian time period.<br /> Using the CoD 2e book I think the area I am most lacking in is supernatural merits for humans. I would love to see this expanded upon (not specifically numina though but that might be interesting as well) and just items in general (which I can probably just come up with using a few lists that are out there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds to me like <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/199275/Chronicles-of-Darkness-Hurt-Locker?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Hurt Locker</a> </b>and the <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/207879/Chronicles-of-Darkness-Dark-Eras-Companion?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Eras Companion</a></b> are what you want!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T23:16:14-08:00","id":1368690,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Dark Eras Companion contains Lifting the Veil, an entire chapter focused on mortals contacting the supernatural, focused around the spiritualist movement of the late 1800s, and Hurt Locker contains additional Supernatural Merits for mortals, both stand-alone powers and clusters of Merits to represent &quot;lesser template&quot; concepts like psychic vampires and sleeper-agent supersoldiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-18T18:50:18-08:00","id":1368835,"title":"","content":"Just grabbed hurt locker and yep this adds a lot of what I needed, even including more supernatural merits (and merits in general). Thanks guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2500-corelogic","name":"Corelogic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}